<mi>&#960;</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math>.&nbsp;Then, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi></math> is :"}, "options": [{"id": "d25601", "text": "increasing in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mi>&#960;</mi><mn>6</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mi>&#960;</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f772ee0e063d9289d2c"}, {"id": "155b8d", "text": "decreasing in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mi>&#960;</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f772ee0e063d9289d2d"}, {"id": "5a2968", "text": "increasing in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mi>&#960;</mi><mn>6</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f772ee0e063d9289d2e"}, {"id": "3d4bb8", "text": "decreasing in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mi>&#960;</mi><mn>6</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f772ee0e063d9289d2f"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f772ee0e063d9289d30", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfb0a"], "topics": ["60ced3320e34b73944ddfad9"], "concepts": ["63d41b25c55fda0b9ff1f7a8"], "question": {"text": "If the function $f(x)=2 x^3-9 \\mathrm{ax}^2+12 \\mathrm{a}^2 \\mathrm{x}+1$, where $\\mathrm{a} \\gt 0$, attains its local maximum and local minimum values at $p$ and $q$, respectively, such that $\\mathrm{p}^2=\\mathrm{q}$, then $f(3)$ is equal to:"}, "options": [{"id": "14cfb0", "text": "55", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f772ee0e063d9289d31"}, {"id": "aa5aa6", "text": "10", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f772ee0e063d9289d32"}, {"id": "713705", "text": "23", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f772ee0e063d9289d33"}, {"id": "b1fca6", "text": "37", "is