ue at $x=\\frac{1}{\\mathrm{e}}$ then :"}, "options": [{"id": "1ba47b", "text": "$\\mathrm{e}^\\pi < \\pi^{\\mathrm{e}}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f772ee0e063d9289d4a"}, {"id": "6dd178", "text": "$\\mathrm{e}^\\pi>\\pi^{\\mathrm{e}}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f772ee0e063d9289d4b"}, {"id": "4deb1a", "text": "$(2 e)^\\pi>\\pi^{(2 e)}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f772ee0e063d9289d4c"}, {"id": "e13b81", "text": "$\\mathrm{e}^{2 \\pi} < (2 \\pi)^{\\mathrm{e}}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f772ee0e063d9289d4d"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f772ee0e063d9289d4e", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfb0a"], "topics": ["60ced5dc19d2aa2b78a3a762"], "concepts": ["60e2fbc066f9ce3f243b54b3"], "question": {"text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>&#34;</mo></msup><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>&#62;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>. If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g</mi></math> is decreasing in the interval <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>&#945;</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;and increasing in the interval <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>, then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>tan</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mn>2</mn><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>tan</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mfenced><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>&#945;</mi></mfrac></mfenced><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>tan</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mfenced><mfrac><mro