></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mn>4</mn></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>.<br />Consider the following two statements:</p><p>(A)&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>&#8804;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>for&#160;all</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>(B)&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>&#8805;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>for&#160;all</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Then,</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "f8618e", "text": "Neither statement <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>)</mo></math> nor statement <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>)</mo></math> is true", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f772ee0e063d9289d6d"}, {"id": "ba740b", "text": "Only statement <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>)</mo></math> is true", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f772ee0e063d9289d6e"}, {"id": "02c8d9", "text": "Both the statements <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>)</mo></math>and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#160;</mo></math>are true", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f772ee0e063d9289d6f"}, {"id": "ac957b", "text": "Only statement <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>)</mo></math> is true", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f772ee0e063d9289d70"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f772ee0e063d9289d71", "